# Solana Risk Radar — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local to use. EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS OPTIONAL: the app runs with
# no configuration at all, no API keys and no accounts.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOLANA_RPC_URL — optional private Solana RPC endpoint
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave this UNSET unless you have a dedicated endpoint.
#
# When unset, the app uses a built-in list of public endpoints that are known to
# serve getTokenLargestAccounts (the method holder-concentration analysis needs,
# which most free tiers block) and fails over between them automatically.
#
# When set, your endpoint is tried FIRST and the public list stays as fallback.
# A dedicated endpoint mainly buys speed and rate-limit headroom: scanning the
# holders of a very large token takes several seconds on public infrastructure.
#
# Do NOT set this to https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com — that endpoint rejects
# getTokenLargestAccounts with HTTP 429 on essentially every request, which
# would push holder analysis to the back of the failover chain for no benefit.
#
# Free tiers that work well: https://helius.dev, https://quicknode.com,
# https://alchemy.com, https://triton.one
#
# SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=your-key-here
#
# This value is read on the server only and is never sent to the browser.

# HELIUS_API_KEY — optional, server-only Activity Intelligence acquisition key.
# Without it, the secondary activity panel returns UNAVAILABLE; the 13-signal
# risk report is unaffected. No key is required to run the app or unit tests.
# Enable Parsed Events access in your Helius account; quotas are plan-specific.
# HELIUS_API_KEY=your-key-here
